  "steps": [
    "Roast the almonds, chana, pumpkin seeds, flax seeds and black sesame seeds until lightly golden, crisp and aromatic. Keep aside.",
    "In the same pan, add 1 tbsp ghee + jaggery and cook on a low flame for around 2 minutes, until the jaggery melts down nicely.",
    "Add the chilli oil and salt and give it a quick mix.",
    "Immediately add all the roasted nuts and seeds and mix really well so everything gets coated evenly.",
    "Quickly transfer onto a plate lined with baking paper and spread it out before the jaggery starts cooling and clumping.",
    "Let it cool completely, then break into clusters and store in an airtight container.",
    "Eat in moderation - Max 2-3 clusters in a day as it is high on cals.",
    "Important: Once the jaggery melts, work very quickly and keep the flame low throughout."
  ],
